    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "dlOO52TdjqCP"
      },
      "source": [
        "#Supervised Learning"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "d62X-rzMuTqH"
      },
      "source": [
        "Supervised learning is a type of machine learning where the model is trained using labeled data, meaning each input comes with a known output. The algorithm learns to map inputs to their correct outputs by finding patterns in the data, allowing it to make predictions on new, unseen examples. For instance, it can learn to classify emails as spam or not spam, or predict house prices based on features like size and location. In short, supervised learning teaches a model by example so it can generalize and make accurate predictions in the future."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "7pHVEzjOjv3J"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Linear Regression"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "G_iryzHaugfW"
      },
      "source": [
        "Linear regression is a supervised learning algorithm used to model the relationship between one or more input variables (called independent variables) and an output variable (called the dependent variable) by fitting a straight line through the data. The goal is to find the line that best predicts the output based on the inputs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 3,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 472
        },
        "id": "Wp5wOPL2jdJP",
        "outputId": "941e1ce0-2fdc-4fbb-9e28-443a8e542d89"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "X_boston, y_boston = datasets.fetch_california_housing(return_X_y=True)\n",
        "X_train_b, X_test_b, y_train_b, y_test_b = train_test_split(X_boston, y_boston, test_size=0.3, random_state=42)\n",
        "linear_regressor = LinearRegression() # Train the Linear Regression\n",
        "linear_regressor.fit(X_train_b[:, :1], y_train_b) # Train the Linear Regression\n",
        "y_pred_b = linear_regressor.predict(X_test_b[:, :1]) # Make predictions\n",
        "\n",
        "# Visualization\n",
        "plt.scatter(X_test_b[:, 0], y_test_b, color='blue', label=\"Actual Data\")\n",
        "plt.plot(X_test_b[:, 0], y_pred_b, color='red', label=\"Predicted Line\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Linear Regression: Predicting House Price from Median Income\")\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Median Income (in tens of thousands of dollars)\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Median House Price (in hundreds of thousands of dollars)\")\n",
        "plt.legend()\n",
        "plt.show()\n"
      ]
    },
